From 4fb64a94f05377b7f521ac61191d9c14f2970188 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Linnard Alex Brown Jr." <labj1987@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:08:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/33] Runtime: serve the console's 2 MiB and 4 MiB pages in
 XMemVirtualAlloc and a title's VirtualAlloc

The console's allocation type picks the page size with bits the host reads
differently: 0x20000000 (2 MiB) is the host's MEM_LARGE_PAGES, which needs
SeLockMemoryPrivilege, 0x80000000 (4 MiB) is rejected, and 0x20400000 (64 KiB)
becomes MEM_LARGE_PAGES | MEM_PHYSICAL. XMemVirtualAlloc failed the 2 MiB mode
and rejected 4 MiB, and the title VirtualAlloc shim forwarded all three.

Both now share one path: the bits are decoded (other combinations stay
ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER), never forwarded, and every page size is served from
ordinary host pages with the base aligned to the page size (VirtualAlloc2 with
an alignment requirement, else a reserve/release/reserve probe with retry),
sizes and addresses rounded to whole pages, and one host allocation per
region so VirtualFree and VirtualQuery match what was returned. A title's
VirtualAlloc still needs an operation; nonzero XMem attribute words still
fail with ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED.

Page-size values as read in OpenScarlett (MIT, kernelx_abi.h, xmemory.cpp) and
omonkeyz/xbox-emulator (GPL-3.0-or-later, crates/compat/xmem/src/virt.rs); the
probe fallback follows xbox-emulator's reserve_aligned (sys.rs).

xmem_test gains 2 MiB / 4 MiB / 64 KiB cases for both entry points (24 of 104
checks fail on main; 146/146 pass here), and xmem_probe reruns it with
LEONIDA_XMEM_NO_VIRTUALALLOC2 set to cover the fallback.

AI-assisted (Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
